use an RTM wrapper if the lock variable is not readable in the wrapper.)>>endobj2639 0 obj<</Dest(G13.75669)/Next 2637 0 R/Parent 2595 0 R/Prev 2596 0 R/Title(8.3.2 Elision Friendly Critical Section Locks)>>endobj2640 0 obj<</Dest(G13.75825)/Parent 2632 0 R/Title(Tuning Suggestion 24. Use an RTM wrapper for locks that implement queuing as part of the initial atomic operation.)>>endobj2641 0 obj<</Count 1/Dest(G13.75811)/First 2642 0 R/Last 2642 0 R/Next 2632 0 R/Parent 2630 0 R/Prev 2643 0 R/Title(8.3.6.3 Implementing Ticket Locks Using Intel® TSX)>>endobj2642 0 obj<</Dest(G13.75818)/Parent 2641 0 R/Title(Tuning Suggestion 23. Use RTM to elide ticket locks.)>>endobj2643 0 obj<</Count 1/Dest(G13.75806)/First 2644 0 R/Last 2644 0 R/Next 2641 0 R/Parent 2630 0 R/Prev 2631 0 R/Title(8.3.6.2 Implementing Reader-Writer Locks Using Intel® TSX)>>endobj2644 0 obj<</Dest(G13.75810)/Parent 2643 0 R/Title(Tuning Suggestion 22. For Read/Write locks elide the complete lock operation, not the building block locks.)>>endobj2645 0 obj<</Dest(G13.76081)/Next 2594 0 R/Parent 2592 0 R/Prev 2646 0 R/Title(8.4.9 HLE Specific Performance Monitoring Events)>>endobj2646 0 obj<</Dest(G13.76068)/Next 2645 0 R/Parent 2592 0 R/Prev 2647 0 R/Title(8.4.8 Profiling and Testing Intel TSX Software sing the Intel® SDE)>>endobj2647 0 obj<</Count 1/Dest(G13.76064)/First 2648 0 R/Last 2648 0 R/Next 2646 0 R/Parent 2592 0 R/Prev 2649 0 R/Title(8.4.7 Last Branch Records and Transactional Aborts)>>endobj2648 0 obj<</Dest(G13.76066)/Parent 2647 0 R/Title(Tuning Suggestion 37. The PEBS profiling handler should support sampling LBRs on abort and report them to the user.)>>endobj2649 0 obj<</Count 3/Dest(G13.76055)/First 2650 0 R/Last 2651 0 R/Next 2647 0 R/Parent 2592 0 R/Prev 2652 0 R/Title(8.4.6 Call Graphs for Transactional Aborts)>>endobj2650 0 obj<</Dest(G13.76061)/Next 2664 0 R/Parent 2649 0 R/Title(Tuning Suggestion 34. The profiler should have options to display ReturnIP and EventingIP.)>>endobj2651 0 obj<</Dest(G13.76063)/Parent 2649 0 R/Prev 2664 0 R/Title(Tuning Suggestion 36. To see function calls inside the transactional region use LBRs or SDE.)>>endobj2652 0 obj<</Count 2/Dest(G13.76017)/First 2653 0 R/Last 2653 0 R/Next 2649 0 R/Parent 2592 0 R/Prev 2654 0 R/Title(8.4.5 XABORT Arguments for RTM Fallback Handlers)>>endobj2653 0 obj<</Count 1/Dest(G13.76025)/First 2663 0 R/Last 2663 0 R/Parent 2652 0 R/Title(XABORT Code)>>endobj2654 0 obj<</Count 6/Dest(G13.75998)/First 2655 0 R/Last 2656 0 R/Next 2652 0 R/Parent 2592 0 R/Prev 2657 0 R/Title(8.4.4 Classifying Aborts Using a Profiling Tool)>>endobj2655 0 obj<</Dest(G13.76007)/Next 2662 0 R/Parent 2654 0 R/Title(Tuning Suggestion 27. The aborts with the highest cost should be examined first.)>>endobj2656 0 obj<</Dest(G13.76016)/Parent 2654 0 R/Prev 2659 0 R/Title(Tuning Suggestion 32. The PEBS TX Abort Information bits should be all displayed by the profiling tool.)>>endobj2657 0 obj<</Dest(G13.75994)/Next 2654 0 R/Parent 2592 0 R/Prev 2658 0 R/Title(8.4.3 Sampling Transactional Aborts)>>endobj2658 0 obj<</Dest(G13.75989)/Next 2657 0 R/Parent 2592 0 R/Prev 2593 0 R/Title(8.4.2 Finding Locks to Elide and Verifying All Locks are Elided.)>>endobj2659 0 obj<</Dest(G13.76015)/Next 2656 0 R/Parent 2654 0 R/Prev 2660 0 R/Title(Tuning Suggestion 31. The profiler should support displaying the ReturnIP with callgraph for non-Instruction abort events, but display the EventingRIP for instruction abort events.)>>endobj2660 0 obj<</Dest(G13.76014)/Next 2659 0 R/Parent 2654 0 R/Prev 2661 0 R/Title(Tuning Suggestion 30. For data conflicts or capacity aborts, concentrate on the whole critical section, not just the instruction address reported at the time of the abort.)>>endobj2661 0 obj<</Dest(G13.76013)/Next 2660 0 R/Parent 2654 0 R/Prev 2662 0 R/Title(Tuning Suggestion 29. Instruction aborts should be analyzed early, but only when they are costly and happe